 ## Overview
 Staged and Alternating Optimization decouples the optimization of coupled parameters (such as geometry, material, lighting, or camera poses) into sequential phases or alternating sub-problems [G]. It distinguishes itself from simultaneous joint optimization methods by preventing gradient interference and local minima, allowing the solver to establish a coarse global alignment or geometric proxy before refining fine-scale details, materials, or uncertain parameters [G].
 
